    verification claimLandCheckRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "66580a1b-dca1-4b7c-a45c-1db198f52e36"; :>> title = "Sprint 427 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-23"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous retro (D0049). AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN under rcRecurrence: no new class - the trusted-authored-timestamp defect is the same family the impossible-evidence-date guard closed for TestResults; the lesson recorded there (bound every authored date by git ancestry) has now been applied to the second surface it was always going to bite, and grep says no third authored-date surface remains unbounded (createdAt is advisory, not ranking). WELL: the panel's interleaving-level findings translated directly into a test fixture - the scratch-repo pattern is reusable for the control-evaluation sprint. Estimate 1 pt, delivered 1."; }
